# fresh_dev_suspend_second_suspend_resume_dies: A second rvg_device_will_suspend and rvg_device_finish_suspend without a resume, and no display page (so no guest display dies): the second blob is written after the first rvg_device_finish_suspend released the root FIFO, so keys 6-8 and 19 (written, read, start, fault offset), which read 0 with no root FIFO (DeviceCore::serialize_suspend_state), are 0, while key 4 still carries the enable mark. rvg_device_will_resume accepts it on a fresh device; in rvg_device_did_resume, DeviceCore::resume_root_fifo's DeviceCore::create_root_fifo refuses start 0 and makes no FIFO, and the resume ends the process (DeviceDeath::ResumedRootFifoMissing): the host dies at rvg_device_did_resume.
